<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?><kml xmlns="http://www.opengis.net/kml/2.2"><Document><name>ILLUSTRATIVE electron-iqps10 ascent</name><description>ILLUSTRATIVE ASCENT ECEF — Electron &#x27;The Mountain God Rises&#x27; (iQPS Launch 10) — NOT OFFICIAL TELEMETRY
Loft: Rocket Lab Electron Payload User Guide 8.0 GENERIC example flight profile (not this mission): altitude knots 0@0s, ~78km@155s (S1 cutoff),
~82km@162s (S2 ignition), ~126km@184s (fairing sep); S2 cutoff L+535s. Source: https://rocketlabcorp.com/assets/Rocket-Lab-Electron-Payload-User-Guide-8.0.pdf
Rocket Lab has published NO flight timeline for The Mountain God Rises (Electron&#x27;s 100th launch); mission page https://rocketlabcorp.com/missions/launches/iqps-the-mountain-god-rises/ gives 575 km LEO, inclination 42 deg.
Assumptions: (a) S2-cutoff altitude set to the published 575 km orbit, altitude linear 184s-&gt;535s;
(b) ground-relative horizontal speed ramps linearly 0 -&gt; 7.223 km/s (circular v at 575 km minus Earth rotation along Az) at 535s.
Real Electron parks in a lower elliptical orbit and the Kick Stage circularizes later (timing unpublished); this file ends at S2 cutoff.
Azimuth: mean bearing from LC-1 to space-debris area centroids HYDROPAC 3249/26 area B -40.46,-174.79 (104.4 deg) and HYDROPAC 3251/26 -41.59,-159.20 (105.0 deg),
2215Z-0700Z daily 13-26 Nov (https://www.space-notices.com/entry/launch-electron-the-mountain-god-rises-iqps-launch-10). Non-rotating i ~41.5 deg vs published 42 deg.
Payload: 1x QPS-SAR (iQPS Launch 10). T0: Rocket Lab launch-safety page &#x27;NET 05:30 UTC | 18:30 NZDT, Saturday 14th November 2026 [NZDT]&#x27; = 2026-11-14T05:30:00Z
(Fri 13 Nov 9:30 pm PST); agrees with LL2 NET (Go). Backup days 14-26 Nov NZT. https://rocketlabcorp.com/launch/launch-safety/
Pad (LL2): -39.260881N 177.865826E. Frame: WGS-84 ECEF, positions km, velocities km/s.
Constant-azimuth rhumb Az=104.68 deg from pad. Velocity ECEF: v_horiz along Az + hdot Up in local ENU.
T0 used: 2026-11-14T05:30:00Z. Re-run with another T0 by shifting utc_iso only; ECEF geometry is Earth-fixed.</description>
